A_561 - Generally, when we think of a road, we think of a paved road and nothing else. Generally, when we think of vegetation, we think of plants or trees and nothing else. Generally, when we think of squares, we think of paving and nothing else. I leave this advice: when thinking of these concepts in your mind, regardless of their location, it's always best to keep in mind that there may very well be abandoned waste nearby. This way, your mental health is generally much better protected. I recommend carrying out periodic patrols and observations of the area using a means of transport that allows for detailed checks (not by car). Furthermore, beyond the potential presence of waste, sometimes there may also be the potential presence of "other" things (animals, etc.) abandoned.